 "title": "Overwatch 2 Retail Patch Notes – March 12, 2024",
 "seq": 1,
 "sections": [
  {
   "type": "generic_update",
   "title": "OVERWATCH 2 X COWBOY BEBOP",
   "role": null,
   "description": "Celebrate the legendary crew of Bebop in Overwatch 2! Immerse yourself in the iconic saga of Cowboy Bebop with an array of new skins found exclusively in the Overwatch 2 shop. From now until March 25, you can also tackle in-game challenges to answer the call of the bounty hunter and snatch up cosmic cosmetic rewards.",
   "heroes": [],
   "blocks": []
  },
  {
   "type": "generic_update",
   "title": "GENERAL UPDATES",
   "role": null,
   "description": null,
   "heroes": [],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "title": "NEW GAME MODE – HERO MASTERY: GAUNTLET",
     "body": "Hero Mastery: Gauntlet is a new co-op game mode where players work together to protect towers from enemy bots. Collect energy and buy powerful upgrades to survive all ten rounds! Focus your skills to earn high scores and compete on the leaderboards. Are you ready to enter the Gauntlet?\n\n- Gauntlet teams can have up to three players and must survive all ten rounds to win. Each game randomizes the upgrades, bots, and targeted towers to keep things fresh.\n- The Gauntlet has four difficulties that vary all aspects of gameplay, including score. Work your way up to Legendary and dominate the leaderboards.\n- Athena has upgraded the simulation with many new bots for this mode. Be on the lookout for dangerous elite training bots.\n- Play with AI mode is available for teams to practice with 1-3 players. Scores and Challenges are not recorded in this mode.\n\nHero Mastery: Gauntlet is launching with a limited-time event that includes exclusive rewards and challenges. Can you defend the towers and unlock them all?",
     "dev": null
    },
    {
     "title": "COMPETITIVE PLAY UPDATES",
     "body": "- Competitive Placements and Overview will now be displayed before Hero Progression at the end of a Competitive Match.\n- Competitive Rank Range has been added to the scoreboard so players can view the rank range of a match at any time.\n- Modifiers can now be viewed outside of the Competitive Overview with a rank info button found on the Competitive Play menu.\n- A new modifier called “Demotion Protection” has been added to the Competitive Overview to notify players that if they lose another game, they will be demoted to the next lowest division.",
     "dev": null
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "generic_update",
   "title": "HERO UPDATES",
   "role": null,
   "description": null,
   "heroes": [],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "title": "PROJECTILE SIZE UPDATES",
     "body": "- Global projectile size modifier for travel time projectiles with a speed greater than 50 meters per second reduced from 0.1 to 0.075 meters.",
     "dev": "Developer Comments: We are decreasing the size of the fastest travel time projectiles because it reduces the frequency of these projectiles failing to headshot due to hitting the enemy's chest hit volume first."
    },
    {
     "title": "ROLE PASSIVES UPDATES",
     "body": "- Heal reduction applied by the damage role passive lowered from 20% to 15%.",
     "dev": "Developer Comments: The Damage role passive reduces the potency of in-combat healing and helps equalize the effectiveness between burst and damage over time. Nevertheless, we are going to experiment with a lower value to relieve some of the pressure on tank and support roles. We’ll be keeping a close eye on this change as we want the healing reduction to still be noticeable."
    },
    {
     "title": "OTHER HERO UPDATES",
     "body": "- Added a new UI element above the player's first-person health bar to show all active healing status effects (Anti-Heal, Amplified Healing, Reduced Healing).",
     "dev": null
    }
   ]
  },
